  <h1>Lunar Listings</h1>
  <p class="meta">NASA Space Apps 2026 &middot; Lunar Landing Site Navigator &middot; Python, NumPy, Numba, React, deck.gl</p>

  <p>The pitch is a joke with a real answer underneath: the UN is selling the Moon, so what would the listings site look like? Each plot gets a price, which we call the Moonstimate, and that price is computed from where the Sun and Earth actually are, what the terrain does to the light, and how steep and cold the ground is.</p>

  <p>
    <a href="https://faletto.com/afc-spaceapps/">Open the site</a>&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/faletto/afc-spaceapps">Source</a>
  </p>

  <figure>
    <img src="/img/lunar-listings-map.jpg" width="1500" height="900" alt="The Lunar Listings map with price markers over a grey lunar surface and a list of plots on the right." />
    <figcaption>The Moon-wide view. Prices on the map and in the list come out of the pipeline.</figcaption>
